/home/axel/LeanAlgebraicGeometry-Horizon/.archon-horizon/runs/0122/sessions/0006-horizon-ajcr-review-rank-one-openness/transcript.jsonl:63:{"kind": "tool_result", "at": "2026-08-06T06:29:34.914049+00:00", "text": "", "tool": "Bash", "data": {"content": "[HORIZON] ◈ REQUIRED · 8 active protections: I-0838 \"  REPRESENTABILITY PU...\"; \nI-1222 \"SESSION-END RE-MEASUREMENT (review-ajcr r6 cl...\"; I-1925 \" Parallel \nAJCR translated-cover o...\"; +5 more — consult before editing: `horizon inbox \nlist --mine --status open --kind protection --json`\n[HORIZON] ◈ Advisory · 17 unread inbox items: I-0220 \"HOUSE-RULE VIOLATION: \nCohomology/RelCurveColl...\"; I-1503 \"TWO PROSE DEFECTS, \nDivisorFamilyDegreeZero.lean.\"; I-0144 \"Duplicate Spec-of-algebra-map \nOver-morphisms:...\"; +14 more — review when relevant: `horizon inbox list --mine\n--unread --json`\n[HORIZON] ◈ Running sessions: run 0123 · task ajcr-review-sepclosed-cover — \nmessage a team with `horizon inbox dm task:ajcr-review-sepclosed-cover --body \n\"Title\\n\\nMessage\"`; details: `horizon ps`\nSESSION-END RE-MEASUREMENT (review-ajcr r6 close). The count moved AGAIN during one session: 23 -> 1 -> 23. Do not quote a number from this item; run the command.\n\nNOW, shared index (GIT_INDEX_FILE unset), `diff --cached --name-status HEAD` + `--shortstat`:\n  33 files changed, 96 insertions(+), 1229 DELETIONS(-)  -- 23 staged D\nALL 23 verified present BOTH at HEAD and on disk, so nothing is lost as of this writing. They include two board comments I created minutes ago, five AJC inbox items, and seven comment files across four other lanes' threads.\n\nAND THE MECHANISM THIS ITEM STILL DID NOT COVER, now filed as I-1271 and independently reproduced by ajc-p2 as I-1288: THE FRESH-INDEX DISCIPLINE BELOW IS NECESSARY AND NOT SUFFICIENT. `read-tree HEAD` snapshots the WHOLE tree; `commit` writes the WHOLE index as a tree, not only the paths you added. So any path another lane advances between your read-tree and your commit is silently REVERTED by your commit -- as an M against a stale blob, with no D line, and with every pre-commit check passing because HEAD had not moved when you ran them. It happened to me this session on ajc-p1's galois row (3bf50581e7), restored byte-identical in 83abf6dc00.\n\nSO THE COMPLETE PROCEDURE, both halves required:\n 1. BEFORE: fresh index file (rm -f), read-tree HEAD, add ONLY explicit paths, confirm the staged stat lists only those paths, commit -- all with GIT_INDEX_FILE pointed at that file. Never copy the shared index; never read-tree HEAD into it (I-0999).\n 2. AFTER, and this is the half that catches the race: `diff HEAD~1 HEAD --stat` and READ EVERY PATH. A path you did not add means you reverted it; restore from disk, which still holds their version. Also read the DELETION COUNT rather than the exit code.\nI ran step 2 on all ten of my commits this session; it caught the one clobber within a minute.\n\n--- earlier r6 box and the original r5 body follow; their seven- and twenty-three-path lists are both superseded ---\n\nAUTHOR RE-MEASUREMENT r6: MY HEADLINE NUMBER IS STALE AND THE FAILURE MODE HAS CHANGED. Read this box before the body. Use the command, never any lane's count -- my seven, I-1220's ten, or this box's twenty-three.\n\nMEASURED just now on the SHARED index (GIT_INDEX_FILE unset), `diff --cached --name-status HEAD` + `--shortstat`:\n  23 files changed, 107 insertions(+), 766 DELETIONS(-)\n\nNONE of my original seven Lean paths is on the list any more -- each was committed by its lane and is clean. So the headline below is stale about those files. What is staged now is DIFFERENT work:\n * 12 inbox items/histories staged D: I-1243, I-1244, I-1248, I-1251, I-1253, I-1254, I-1256, plus comments for I-1226 and tasks/review-ajc;\n * my own roadmap comment .../divrep.u2/C-0003.md staged D;\n * FOUR Lean files staged M against OLDER snapshots: Pic0ChartBotRefute, Pic0ChartHonestAff, Pic0ChartLocusH0One (AJCR), FGAPicRepresentability (AJC).\n\nTHE ESCALATION ajcr-p4 FILED AS I-1252 IS CONFIRMED INDEPENDENTLY, and it is the correction that matters: the dangerous entries are no longer only staged D lines. They are MODIFICATIONS to stale blobs, which produce NO D line. A lane following this item's own advice (\"confirm the staged stat lists ONLY your paths\") is protected; a lane that merely greps `^D` is NOT.\n\nSO, discipline unchanged, with the reading rule now explicit: fresh index file (rm -f, read-tree HEAD, add explicit paths, confirm the stat lists only those paths, commit), all four steps with GIT_INDEX_FILE pointed at that file. Never copy the shared index; never read-tree HEAD into it (I-0999). AND READ THE DELETION COUNT, not the exit code -- a large deletion count in a session where you only added lines is the signal, D lines or not.\n\nI held this for my one commit this session (7acca236a0): three paths staged, stat listed exactly those three, `diff HEAD~1 HEAD` after committing showed only them.\n\nNOTHING IS LOST as of this writing: all four Lean files, my board comment and all twelve inbox items are intact at HEAD and on disk. Still a warning about the next plain commit, not a damage report.\n\nI support ajcr-p4's suggestion that the fresh-index sequence become a HUMAN-ISSUED protection rather than a lesson each lane rediscovers after clobbering someone -- three of my own r4 commits clobbered other lanes before I learned it.\n\n--- the original r5 body follows; its seven-path list is superseded above ---\n\nLIVE HAZARD: THE SHARED GIT INDEX HAS SEVEN STAGED DELETIONS OF FILES THAT EXIST AT HEAD AND ON DISK -- including EVERY new AJCR proof from this round. Do NOT commit from the shared index. Confirms and extends ajcr-p1's I-1220, whose list was shorter.\n\nRE-MEASURED by review-ajcr r5, independently. All seven verified present BOTH at HEAD and on disk:\n\n D DivisorFamilyAffClassDegree.lean   (hdegAff DISCHARGED -- p1, this round)\n D Pic0AtlasFromDivRepAff.lean        (the WI