en O') (h : O' \\\\u2264 O) (L : Z.CechPic) : O'.cechPicClass hO' L = CommRing.Pic.mapRingHom (Z.presheaf.map (homOfLE h).op).hom (O.cechPicClass hO L)\\\",\\n    \\\"doc\\\": \\\"**The restriction seam of the affine-open class**: for affine opens `O' \\\\u2264 O`, the class of the restriction to `O'` is the image of the class on `O` under the restriction map of ambient sections \\\\u2014 the `appLE` square of the two inclusions.\\\",\\n    \\\"library\\\": \\\"Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge-Rebuild\\\",\\n    \\\"file\\\": \\\"MainProjects/Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge-Rebuild/AlgebraicJacobian/Picard/EffectivityMoving.lean\\\",\\n    \\\"line\\\": 121,\\n    \\\"score\\\": 20.6944\\n  },\\n  {\\n    \\\"name\\\": \\\"AlgebraicGeometry.isIso_fromTilde\\\\u0393_of_genSections\\\",\\n    \\\"kind\\\": \\\"lemma\\\",\\n    \\\"signature\\\": \\\"lemma isIso_fromTilde\\\\u0393_of_genSections (F : (Spec R).Modules) (\\\\u03c3 : F.GeneratingSections) (\\\\u03c4 : (kernel \\\\u03c3.\\\\u03c0).GeneratingSections) : IsIso F.fromTilde\\\\u0393\\\",\\n    \\\"doc\\\": \\\"**01I8 steps (2)\\\\u2013(3), packaged.**  If an `\\\\ud835\\\\udcaa_{Spec R}`-module `F` is globally generated (`\\\\u03c3 : F.GeneratingSections`, a global epimorphism `free \\\\u03c3.I \\\\u27f6 F`) and the kernel of that epimorphism is itself globally generated (`\\\\u03c4 : (kernel \\\\u03c3.\\\\u03c0).GeneratingSections`), then the tilde\\\\u2013\\\\u0393 counit `tilde (\\\\u0393 F) \\\\u27f6 F` is an isomorphism.  This bundles the two generating families into a global `F.Presentation` and feeds it to Mathlib's `isIso_fromTilde\\\\u0393_of_presentation`; it is the formal content of steps (2)\\\\u2013(3) of the 01I8 decomposition.  The single remaining mathematical input is the affine global-generation theorem (step (1)) producing `\\\\u03c3` and `\\\\u03c4` for a quasi-coherent `F`.  Project-local because it repackages the Mathlib presentation criterion in the two-generating-families form the 01I8 route c