the alternating difference of restrictions of honest sections.\\\",\\n    \\\"library\\\": \\\"Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge\\\",\\n    \\\"file\\\": \\\"MainProjects/Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge/AlgebraicJacobian/Cohomology/CechCoboundarySplitting.lean\\\",\\n    \\\"line\\\": 262,\\n    \\\"score\\\": 20.2693\\n  },\\n  {\\n    \\\"name\\\": \\\"AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.AffineCoverMVSquare.cechKerProj\\\",\\n    \\\"kind\\\": \\\"def\\\",\\n    \\\"signature\\\": \\\"noncomputable def AffineCoverMVSquare.cechKerProj : LinearMap.ker (cechD12 S.coverFamily F).hom \\\\u2192\\\\u2097[k] F.obj.obj (op S.overlapOpen)\\\",\\n    \\\"doc\\\": \\\"The projection of a 1-cocycle to its `(0,1)`-component, transported to the overlap sections.  This is the inverse direction of the kernel identification.\\\",\\n    \\\"library\\\": \\\"Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge\\\",\\n    \\\"file\\\": \\\"MainProjects/Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge/AlgebraicJacobian/RiemannRoch/Adelic/Cokernel.lean\\\",\\n    \\\"line\\\": 912,\\n    \\\"score\\\": 20.1922\\n  },\\n  {\\n    \\\"name\\\": \\\"AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.cechPicMapEquivOfIso\\\",\\n    \\\"kind\\\": \\\"def\\\",\\n    \\\"signature\\\": \\\"noncomputable def cechPicMapEquivOfIso (f : X \\\\u27f6 Y) [IsIso f] : Y.CechPic \\\\u2243* X.CechPic\\\",\\n    \\\"doc\\\": \\\"**(T3-4): the \\\\u010cech Picard groups of isomorphic schemes are isomorphic, ALONG the given isomorphism.**  Stated as a `MulEquiv` rather than as the two `Function.Injective`/`Surjective` faces because a kernel comparison must travel in both directions (`I-0571`): a bare bijection of the two ends of a map is not usable, and what makes this one usable is that it *is* `CechPic.map f`, so it commutes with everything `CechPic.map` commutes with by `map_comp`.\\\",\\n    \\\"library\\\": \\\"Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge-Rebuild\\\",\\n    \\\"file\\\": \\\"MainProjects/Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge-Rebuild/AlgebraicJacobian/Tangent/CechPicIsoTransport.lean\\\",\\n    \\\