ology.lean:89:theorem h0_divisorSheaf_eq_of_picClass_eq {D D' : X.CurveDivisor}\\nAlgebraicJacobian/RiemannRoch/ClassCohomology.lean:92:  Sheaf.h0_congr (picClassDivisorSheafIso K h)\\nAlgebraicJacobian/RiemannRoch/ClassCohomology.lean:95:`h\\u00b9(\\ud835\\udcaa(D))`. Carbon copy of `chi_divisorSheaf_eq_of_picClass_eq` with `Sheaf.h1_congr` in place of\\n=== free glued sheaf iso structure sheaf\\nAlgebraicJacobian/RiemannRoch/DivisorSheafZero.lean:15:* `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.divisorSheafZeroIso : divisorSheaf K 0 \\u2245 X.moduleKSheaf K`.\\nAlgebraicJacobian/RiemannRoch/DivisorSheafZero.lean:279:    X.moduleKSheaf K \\u2245 divisorSheaf K 0 :=\\nAlgebraicJacobian/RiemannRoch/DivisorSheafZero.lean:286:    divisorSheaf K (0 : X.CurveDivisor) \\u2245 X.moduleKSheaf K :=\", \"parent_tool_use_id\": \"toolu_bdrk_01CNdezng5TdGwMcxprDWDY3\", \"subagent_type\": \"general-purpose\"}, \"usage\": null, \"_cursor\": 282544}, {\"kind\": \"tool_call\", \"at\": \"2026-07-30T22:25:23.395000+00:00\", \"text\": \"\", \"tool\": \"Bash\", \"data\": {\"input\": {\"command\": \"sed -n '/\\\\/-!/,/^-\\\\*\\\\//p' AlgebraicJacobian/Tangent/CollapseCechH1.lean | head -60; echo \\\"=== DECLS\\\"; grep -n \\\"^\\\\(theorem\\\\|lemma\\\\|def\\\\|noncomputable def\\\\)\\\" AlgebraicJacobian/Tangent/CollapseCechH1.lean\", \"description\": \"Read CollapseCechH1 header\"}, \"parent_tool_use_id\": \"toolu_bdrk_01CNdezng5TdGwMcxprDWDY3\", \"subagent_type\": \"general-purpose\", \"model\": \"claude-opus-5\"}, \"usage\": {\"tokens_in\": 27006, \"tokens_out\": 1, \"cached_tokens_in\": 0, \"reasoning_tokens_out\": 0, \"cost_usd\": null}, \"_cursor\": 286396}, {\"kind\": \"tool_call\", \"at\": \"2026-07-30T22:25:24.746000+00:00\", \"text\": \"\", \"tool\": \"Bash\", \"data\": {\"input\": {\"command\": \"ls informal/ | head -60; echo \\\"===\\\"; grep -rln \\\"P1_B\\\\|\\u2119\\u00b9_T\\\\|Pic(\\u2119\\u00b9\\\\|pulled back from the base\\\" informal/ blueprint/ 2>/dev/null | head -20\", \"description\": \"Search informal dir for P1 relative Pic route\"}, \"parent_tool_use_id\": \"toolu_bdrk_01CNdezng5TdGwMcxprDWDY3\", \"subagent_type\": \"general-purpose\", \"model\": \"claude-opus-5\"}, \"usage\": {\"tokens_in\": 27006, \"tokens_out\": 1, \"cached_tokens_in\": 0, \"reasoning_tokens_out\": 0, \"cost_usd\": null}, \"_cursor\": 287021}, {\"kind\": \"tool_result\", \"at\": \"2026-07-30T22:25:26.724000+00:00\", \"text\": \"\", \"tool\": \"\", \"data\": {\"content\": \"/-!\\n# (T3-5): the downstairs `k \\u2192 k` \\u010cech `\\u021e\\u00b9` translation (W5-T3)\\n\\nThe seam `informal/w5-t4-worksheet.md` \\u00a77.6 found by printing the types of the arrows T3's\\ncomposition has to join. (T3-2) (`Tangent/EpsArrowIdentification.lean`) matched their **sources**;\\ntheir **targets** are sections of *different schemes*:\\n\\n```\\nengine  (TwoCover.unitsReduction C.left U\\u2080 U\\u2081) lands on   \\u0393(C.left,       U\\u2080 \\u2293 U\\u2081)\\u02e3 \\u29f8 \\u2026\\ngeometry (pullbackOverlapQuot (relCurveMap \\u2026))  lands on   \\u0393(relCurve C k, fst\\u207b\\u00b9U\\u2080 \\u2293 fst\\u207b\\u00b9U\\u2081)\\u02e3 \\u29f8 \\u2026\\n```\\n\\nThis file is the `MulEquiv` between them \\u2014 the `k \\u2192 k` analogue of\\n`Over.dualNumberCechH1Equiv`, built the same way from the same two inputs.\\n\\n## What it is built over, and why NOT the object this lane coined for the job\\n\\n`Tangent/EpsChartSquare.lean`'s `epsChartDown` is a ring equivalence of the right shape, but at\\n**one** open and under `IsAffineOpen`. The right input is **`sectionsCollapse`**\\n(`Cohomology/RelThetaTransportCore.lean:41`), landed for the relative-theta work: a `k`-linear\\nequivalence `\\u0393(C.left, V) \\u2243\\u2097[k] \\u0393(relCurve C k, fst \\u207b\\u00b9\\u1d41 V)` at **arbitrary** `V` with only\\ncompact/quasi-separated hypotheses, **no affineness**, and shipping exactly the two auxiliary lemmas\\nthis construction needs:\\n\\n* `sectionsCollapse_mul` (:116) \\u2014 multiplicativity, hence the units form;\\n* `sectionsCollapse_resHom` (:235) \\u2014 naturality in the open, hence the coboundary image.\\n\\nWorksheet \\u00a77.6 records that the first draft of that section priced this seam by `epsChartDown` and\\ncalled the downstairs side one-third equipped. **Searching the object's shape across the project\\nrather than the name this lane coined found a stronger input with both lemmas already proved.**\\n\\n## Implementation notes \\u2014 one real wall, and it was not an instance\\n\\n`QuotientGroup.congr _ _ e he` is how `Over.dualNumberCechH1Equiv` is built, and copying that\\nspelling here fails with *\\\"failed to synthesize instance \\u2026 `.Normal`\\\"*. Three attempts to supply the\\ninstance were wasted: a `haveI`, a project-local `Subgroup.normal_of_isMulCommutative` instance, and\\ndropping `Scheme.overModule` from the local instances. **None of them was the problem.**\\nMeasured: the\\n`Normal` instance for the exact subgroup synthesizes by `inferInstance` in a standalone probe,\\nand so\\ndoes the quotient *type*. The failure came from the two positional `_`s \\u2014 with the subgroups left as\\nmetavariables, elaboration reaches the `[Normal]` argument before they are solved. Naming **both**\\nsubgroups explicitly in the `congr` call closes it with no instance work at all.\\n\\n> The upstairs file gets away with `_ _` because its own elaboration order happens to solve them\\n> first. A spelling that works in one file is not thereby a spelling; and *\\\"failed to synthesize\\n> instance\\\"* is not always about instances \\u2014 check whether the instance's arguments are still\\n> metavariables. (`I-0685` family; the reverse of `measure-the-instance-surface`.)\\n\\n## Scope\\n\\nEverything here is over the **identity** base change `k \\u2192 k`. It says nothing about a general\\ncoefficient extension, and it is not the dual-number side (that is\\n`Tangent/DualNumberCarrier*.lean`). It does not compose the chain: (T3-6), the composite\\n`H\\u00b9(C,\\ud835\\udcaa) \\u2243+ ker(CechPic(C_\\u03b5) \\u2192 CechPic(C))`, is still unwritten, and whether it comes out\\n**additive** without extra work is unmeasured \\u2014 see worksheet \\u00a77.6.\\n\\n## Main declarations\\n\\n* `AlgebraicGeometry.collapseRingEquiv` / `collapseUnits` \\u2014 the ring and units forms of\\n=== DECLS\\n98:noncomputable def collapseRingEquiv (V : C.left.Opens)\\n106:noncomputable def collapseUnits (V : C.left.Opens)\\n113:theorem unitsMap_resHom_collapseUnits {W V : C.left.Opens} (hWV : W \\u2264 V)\\n136:theorem range_collapseUnits_comp {W W' : C.left.Opens}\\n160:theorem map_cechCoboundaryUnits_collapseUnits\\n188:noncomputable def collapseCechH1Equiv\\n214:theorem collapseCechH1Equiv_mk\", \"parent_tool_use_id\": \"toolu_bdrk_01CNdezng5TdGwMcxprDWDY3\", \"subagent_type\": \"general-purpose\"}, \"usage\": null, \"_cursor\": 287603}, {\"kind\": \"tool_result\", \"at\": \"2026-07-30T22:25:29.852000+00:00\", \"text\": \"\", \"tool\": \"\", \"data\": {\"content\": \"README.md\\napi-chi-cohomology.md\\napi-chi-devissage.md\\napi-chi-divisors.md\\napi-chi-genus.md\\nc1-etale-separatedness-assembly.md\\nc2-effectivity-assembly.md\\nchi-ledger-design.md\\nchi-ledger-notes.md\\ndat-d-worksheet.md\\ndd-f-probe-verdict.md\\ndeg-d2-meromorphic-worksheet.md\\ndeg-d4-recon.md\\ndeg-d4b-worksheet.md\\ndeg-d5b-worksheet.md\\ndegree-pic0-recon.md\\nfiniteness-plan.md\\nledger-index-stale-run0071-s0016.txt\\nm33-spec.md\\nold-draft-picard-recon.md\\npic-affine-dictionary-design.md\\nprotocol-concurrent-lanes.md\\nroute-decision.md\\nsession-handoff-2026-07-12.md\\nsession-handoff-2026-07-14.md\\nsession-handoff-2026-07-14b.md\\nsession-handoff-2026-07-15.md\\nsession-prompt-2026-07-13.md\\nspec-c2-e1.md\\nspec-chi-g8-g9.md\\nspec-dat-1.md\\nspec-dat-6.md\\nspec-dat-a.md\\nspec-datg0.md\\nspec-dd-1.md\\nspec-dd-2.md\\nspec-dd-3.md\\nspec-dd-r.md\\nspec-dd1-pt-seam.md\\nspec-dd4-fieldvanishing.md\\nspec-dd4-redesign.md\\nspec-